From dd552e5c0f34b965d8e1dd276a488323a2415ca8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 17:20:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(traits): keep list-carried traits; import the Explorer
 trait cache with zero REST

The collection list endpoint returns `traits` on each item (verified for
Argonauts from SpencerTinker's raw pull, 8,798 tokens in 44 reads). The list
pass stored name/image/metadata_url only and left 9,161 tokens to the
per-token fallback -- ~76 h of the shared 120/hr budget. list_tokens() now
stores list-carried traits at once (traits_source=opensea_nft_list); the
metadata_url and fallback paths remain for entries that carry none. The
module docstring states what is verified and for which collection.

`navanax import-traits <tokens.json> --collection argonauts` loads the
Explorer cache into tokens/traits: inserts missing tokens, writes traits for
tokens that have none with traits_at = the cache's own generated time, never
overwrites a token that already has traits but diffs it per trait_type and
exits 1 on any disagreement. Idempotent; exact counts. Only `traits` is read
from the cache -- rank/rarity/price are that tool's assumptions.

Requirement: REQ-D-01, REQ-F-07a
Bug: BUG-20260909-049

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011A8nXFkj5HLVG3EBgXf2RU
---
 docs/logs/BUGS.md     |  14 +++-
 docs/logs/BUGS.xlsx   | Bin 47720 -> 48833 bytes
 docs/logs/bugs.yaml   |  28 ++++++++
 src/navanax/cli.py    |  63 ++++++++++++++++++
 src/navanax/traits.py | 145 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 tests/selftest.py     | 125 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 367 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/logs/BUGS.md b/docs/logs/BUGS.md
index b0c4ad6..1285f9d 100644
--- a/docs/logs/BUGS.md
+++ b/docs/logs/BUGS.md
@@ -468,14 +468,26 @@ known defects — not a discovery, and not a new bug.
 |---|---|---|---|---|
 | BUG-20260909-052 | S1 | P0 | fixed | A gap left open by a dead run was never closed — one stale record masked every chart to infinity; launchd restarts made it routine |
 | BUG-20260909-053 | S1 | P0 | fixed | `order_lives` inferred expiry at a time that had not arrived — standing orders recorded as ended, lifetimes biased long |
+| BUG-20260909-054 | S3 | P1 | fixed | The collection list endpoint carries `traits`; the list pass discarded them and left 9,161 tokens to a ~76-hour per-token fallback |
 
 Both found by the tech-lead reproducing the change by running it, both in the
 flattering direction (a quiet market; a durable book), both fixed the same hour
 with a test that failed first.
 
+Found by reading a second tool's scraper against ours. `SpencerTinker/scrape.py`
+reads `nft["traits"]` from the SAME `GET /collection/{slug}/nfts` pages that
+`traits.py` walked on 2026-09-09, and got traits for all 8,798 indexed
+Argonauts in 44 reads. Our docstring said the field was not there; the code
+believed the docstring; the fixture was written from the docstring. The
+47 reads were spent and the field thrown away. Fix: store list-carried
+traits immediately (`opensea_nft_list`), keep the metadata_url / fallback
+paths only for entries without them, and add `navanax import-traits` so the
+friend's cache loads with zero reads. Docstring now states what is verified
+and for which collection; other collections must be re-verified.
+
 ### Still open
 
-**None.** All 53 logged bugs are fixed.
+**None.** All 54 logged bugs are fixed.
 
 ### The lesson
 
